# Where Your Money Goes
> This project isn't about making money. I'm doing my best to be as transparent as possible with the costs and keep your price as low as I can.

## Pricing Logic
Here's the thinking behind the price:

1. **Cover the basics** -- hardware and all the direct costs.
1. **Prepare for possible extra costs** -- for example, tax-related expenses (if they come up), or the cost of acquiring, maintaining, or replacing the test units I use for development and debugging.
1. **Experiment a little** -- give me room to try new ideas for improvements.
1. **Give back** -- to support the FOSS that this project relies on, a portion of the money will be donated to them. (More details on how this is done will be shared after the project has been running for a while and once there's a clearer picture of actual ongoing costs.)

<br>
